### Inverted-index JSON service — request samples
### Base URL defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8080

### Create a document (auto-assigned id)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "inverted index segment merge demo"}

### Create with an explicit id
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{"id": 500, "text": "segment merge policy note"}

### Update the same id — generation advances by one
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{"id": 500, "text": "segment merge policy revised"}

### Read the current live revision
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/documents/500

### Term query
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/search?q=segment

### Boolean AND (both terms in the same revision)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/search
Content-Type: application/json

{"q": "AND:segment,merge"}

### Boolean OR
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/search?q=OR:cafe,rocket

### Force the RAM buffer to flush into a new segment
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/flush

### Merge all published segments
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/merge

### Segment / tombstone counters
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/stats

### Delete the current revision
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8080/documents/500
